Things this project would like to be better. Not issues -- issues are blueprints
for building something. These are wishes, and some of them may never become
anything.

--

I would like a dune to mean something to a tank. Not "terrain type: sand" but a
ridge you crest and are suddenly seen from three kilometres away, and a hollow you
sit in and are not. If sightlines are the paradigm, the ground has to be the thing
you are thinking about the whole time, and it has to be readable at a glance.

I would like the pattern drawn in the sand to feel like a promise. You draw it,
the factory reads it, and every tank that ever rolls off that line keeps it. A
player who drew badly should be able to see, ten minutes later, exactly where the
line goes wrong -- and be unable to fix it without building a new factory.

I would like the dogfight cloud to be watchable the way a fish tank is watchable.
Not information-dense. A thing you glance at while your hands are doing something
else, and can read the mood of without counting anything.

I would like the energy menu to be four buttons and never a fifth. The moment it
grows a fifth, the economy has stopped being about inflows and outflows and
started being about a menu.

I would like the same match to run on a handheld in one hand and on a laptop
across the table, and for neither player to be able to tell which the other has.

I would like the generated dunes to look like a place. Randomly generated and
AI-textured is the mechanism; "it looks like a place" is the wish, and the
mechanism does not guarantee it.

I would like the terminal viewer to still be useful in five years.
